cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use omnitool, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "omnitool: a common GPU ensemble ODE core"
type: software
version: 0.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/spencermcbridemoore/omnitool"
authors:
  - family-names: "McBride Moore"
    given-names: "Spencer"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
keywords:
  - ordinary differential equations
  - GPU
  - CUDA
  - ensemble integration
  - Runge-Kutta
abstract: >-
  omnitool integrates many independent members of an ODE ensemble on a GPU
  with per-member adaptive stepping, dense output at shared save times, FP32
  and FP64 as first-class configurations, and a verification layer that is
  independent of the device code. Physics packages attach through thin,
  optional adapters.
